<section class="fp-hero"><div class="fp-w"><div class="fp-hero-card"><div class="fp-hero-t"><p class="fp-k">Comfort starts underfoot</p><h1>The right sock makes every shoe feel better.</h1><p>Footpad is an independent guide to sock comfort. Find out where you need cushioning, how to wash each fibre so it lasts and which height suits your shoes.</p><p class="fp-acts"><a class="btn" href="#tools">Try the sock tools</a><a class="fp-lnk" href="sock-cushioning-guide.html">Cushioning explained</a></p></div><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1794208248708-303a1b748176?auto=format&fit=crop&w=720&h=600&q=75" alt="feet in patterned wool socks resting on a floor" width="720" height="600" fetchpriority="high"></figure></div></div></section>

<section class="fp-s"><div class="fp-w"><p class="fp-k fp-ctr">Look inside</p><h2 class="fp-ctr">Six parts of a well-made sock</h2><div class="fp-anat"><ul><li><b>Cuff</b>Ribbed and elastic, so it stays up without squeezing.</li><li><b>Instep panel</b>A thinner, open knit across the top of the foot for ventilation.</li><li><b>Arch band</b>A snug ring of elastic that stops the sock twisting.</li></ul><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1794208248591-d029fed3cbe1?auto=format&fit=crop&w=520&h=620&q=75" alt="three people in patterned socks relaxing" width="520" height="620" loading="lazy"></figure><ul><li><b>Heel pocket</b>A shaped cup, often in a Y stitch, that keeps the heel in place.</li><li><b>Terry sole</b>Tiny loops of yarn underfoot that absorb impact and moisture.</li><li><b>Flat toe seam</b>Joined by hand or machine so there is no ridge across the toes.</li></ul></div></div></section>

<section class="fp-s fp-aqua" id="tools"><div class="fp-w"><p class="fp-k">Free tools</p><h2>Three quick sock answers</h2>
<div class="fp-tool"><div class="fp-tool-h"><span>1</span><div><h3>Cushion Zone Picker</h3><p>Where the padding should be for what you do.</p></div></div><div class="fp-row"><label for="cz-a">Most of the day I am<select id="cz-a"><option value="walk">Walking</option><option value="stand">Standing at work</option><option value="run">Running</option><option value="hike">Hiking</option><option value="sit">Sitting at a desk</option><option value="cycle">Cycling</option></select></label><label for="cz-s">My shoes are<select id="cz-s"><option value="roomy">Roomy</option><option value="snug">Snug</option></select></label></div><div class="fp-out" id="cz-o" aria-live="polite"></div></div>
<div class="fp-tool"><div class="fp-tool-h"><span>2</span><div><h3>Wash Settings Finder</h3><p>The right cycle for the fibre and the colour.</p></div></div><div class="fp-row"><label for="ws-f">Fibre<select id="ws-f"><option value="cotton">Cotton</option><option value="wool">Merino or wool</option><option value="synth">Synthetic sport</option><option value="bamboo">Bamboo</option><option value="mix">Mixed or not sure</option></select></label><label for="ws-c">Colour<select id="ws-c"><option value="white">White</option><option value="dark">Dark</option><option value="bright">Bright or patterned</option></select></label><label for="ws-d">How dirty<select id="ws-d"><option value="day">Everyday wear</option><option value="sport">Sweaty or muddy</option></select></label></div><div class="fp-out" id="ws-o" aria-live="polite"></div></div>
<div class="fp-tool"><div class="fp-tool-h"><span>3</span><div><h3>Sock Height Matcher</h3><p>Which cuff height works with your shoes today.</p></div></div><div class="fp-row"><label for="hm-s">Shoes<select id="hm-s"><option value="trainer">Low trainers</option><option value="loafer">Loafers or boat shoes</option><option value="dress">Smart lace-ups</option><option value="ankle">Ankle boots</option><option value="hike">Hiking boots</option><option value="sandal">Sandals</option></select></label><label for="hm-l">Worn with<select id="hm-l"><option value="long">Full-length trousers</option><option value="crop">Cropped trousers</option><option value="short">Shorts</option><option value="skirt">A skirt or dress</option></select></label></div><div class="fp-out" id="hm-o" aria-live="polite"></div></div>
</div></section>

<section class="fp-s"><div class="fp-w fp-two"><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1785692258374-e7c5f06494ba?auto=format&fit=crop&w=600&h=560&q=75" alt="white trainers and striped socks casting a long shadow" width="600" height="560" loading="lazy"></figure><div><p class="fp-k">How much padding?</p><h2>Four levels of cushion</h2><dl class="fp-lv"><div><dt>None</dt><dd>Thin all over. Dress shoes, loafers and hot days.</dd></div><div><dt>Light</dt><dd>A fine terry layer under heel and ball. Everyday trainers.</dd></div><div><dt>Medium</dt><dd>Fuller terry along the whole sole. Long walks and standing work.</dd></div><div><dt>Full</dt><dd>Padding underfoot and around the ankle. Hiking boots and cold weather.</dd></div></dl></div></div></section>

<section class="fp-s fp-navy"><div class="fp-w"><p class="fp-k">Wash day</p><h2>Five habits that double a sock&rsquo;s life</h2><ol class="fp-five"><li><b>Inside out</b>Wash them turned, so the inside is cleaned and the outside does not pill.</li><li><b>Cool water</b>Thirty degrees protects the elastic and the colour.</li><li><b>No softener</b>It coats fibres and stops them wicking moisture.</li><li><b>Mesh bag</b>Keeps pairs together and prevents stretching.</li><li><b>Line dry</b>Heat from a dryer is the main cause of slack cuffs.</li></ol></div></section>

<section class="fp-s"><div class="fp-w"><p class="fp-k">Guides</p><h2>Two full guides</h2><div class="fp-gds"><a href="sock-cushioning-guide.html"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1788434070598-c3cdd7e9a2fd?auto=format&fit=crop&w=640&h=380&q=75" alt="person wearing black trainers and green socks" width="640" height="380" loading="lazy"><div><h3>The Sock Cushioning Guide</h3><p>Terry loops, padding zones, toe seams and arch bands: what each does and who needs it.</p><span>Read guide &rarr;</span></div></a><a href="sock-washing-guide.html"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1788278271485-a13b37cf1ff0?auto=format&fit=crop&w=640&h=380&q=75" alt="hand-knitted wool garments hanging on a clothesline" width="640" height="380" loading="lazy"><div><h3>The Sock Washing Guide</h3><p>Sorting, temperatures, drying and stain fixes for cotton, wool, bamboo and sports socks.</p><span>Read guide &rarr;</span></div></a></div></div></section>

<section class="fp-s fp-aqua"><div class="fp-w"><p class="fp-k">At a glance</p><h2>Which sock for which shoe</h2><div class="tblw"><table class="fp-tbl"><thead><tr><th>Shoe</th><th>Height</th><th>Cushion</th><th>Fibre</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Low trainers</td><td>Ankle or quarter</td><td>Light</td><td>Cotton or synthetic blend</td></tr><tr><td>Running shoes</td><td>Ankle with heel tab</td><td>Light, targeted</td><td>Synthetic, seamless toe</td></tr><tr><td>Loafers</td><td>No-show</td><td>None</td><td>Fine cotton with grip heel</td></tr><tr><td>Smart lace-ups</td><td>Mid-calf</td><td>None</td><td>Fine cotton or merino</td></tr><tr><td>Ankle boots</td><td>Crew</td><td>Light to medium</td><td>Merino blend</td></tr><tr><td>Hiking boots</td><td>Crew or higher</td><td>Medium to full</td><td>Merino blend</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></section>

<section class="fp-s"><div class="fp-w fp-two fp-two-r"><div><p class="fp-k">Getting dressed</p><h2>Three rules for socks that show</h2><ul class="fp-rules"><li><b>With a suit,</b> the sock matches the trousers and is long enough that no skin shows when you sit.</li><li><b>With jeans,</b> pick up one colour from your top or jacket, or go bold on purpose.</li><li><b>With shorts,</b> either show the sock properly, as a crew, or hide it completely. Half-visible looks accidental.</li></ul></div><div class="fp-pics"><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1794562385717-d187035420d3?auto=format&fit=crop&w=420&h=520&q=75" alt="person in a black suit putting on black dress socks" width="420" height="520" loading="lazy"></figure><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1788713756341-4a0d98b0ff9f?auto=format&fit=crop&w=420&h=520&q=75" alt="person wearing a purple knitted sock" width="420" height="520" loading="lazy"></figure></div></div></section>

<section class="fp-s fp-aqua"><div class="fp-w fp-fq"><p class="fp-k fp-ctr">FAQ</p><h2 class="fp-ctr">Common sock questions</h2><div class="fp-faq"><details open><summary>Where should a sock be cushioned?</summary><p>Under the heel and the ball of the foot, where your weight lands with every step. Walkers and hikers benefit from padding in both places; for office wear, a thin, uncushioned sock usually feels better in a close-fitting shoe.</p></details><details><summary>Are cushioned socks too hot for summer?</summary><p>They can be if the whole sock is thick. Look for socks that are padded only underfoot, with a thin, open-knit panel across the top of the foot to let heat out.</p></details><details><summary>What temperature should I wash socks at?</summary><p>Thirty degrees is enough for almost every sock and is kindest to the elastic. Use forty for heavily soiled cotton sports socks. Wool should always be washed cool on a gentle cycle.</p></details><details><summary>Why do my socks lose their stretch?</summary><p>Heat. A hot wash and, above all, a hot tumble dryer break down the elastane fibres that hold the sock&rsquo;s shape. Wash cool, skip the fabric softener and dry on a line.</p></details><details><summary>Which sock height goes with ankle boots?</summary><p>A crew sock that reaches above the top of the boot. A sock that ends below the boot collar lets the leather rub directly on the skin.</p></details><details><summary>Should socks match shoes or trousers?</summary><p>For smart outfits, match the trousers, which makes the leg look longer. For casual outfits you are free: pick up a colour from elsewhere in what you are wearing, or let the socks be the one bright thing.</p></details></div></div></section>

<section class="fp-s"><div class="fp-w"><div class="fp-nl"><div><h2>The Footpad Note</h2><p>One comfort tip and one care reminder each month. Short and useful.</p></div><a class="btn" href="mailto:hello@footpad.com?subject=The%20Footpad%20Note&amp;body=Please%20subscribe%20me.">Subscribe by email</a></div></div></section>

